# Token Billing Service

Spring Boot app that calculates LLM token usage bills. Primary spec: `requirements/token-usage-billing-story.md`.

## Stack

- Java 21, Gradle, Spring Boot 3.5
- Spring Web, Validation, Data JPA
- Flyway migrations (`src/main/resources/db/migration/`)
- PostgreSQL (runtime); H2 available for tests only
- Lombok allowed (already on classpath)

## Run locally

```bash
docker compose up -d          # Postgres on localhost:54323, db token_billing
./gradlew bootRun             # default http://localhost:8080
./gradlew test
```

Datasource (from `application.yml`): `jdbc:postgresql://localhost:54323/token_billing`, user/password `postgres`. JPA `ddl-auto: validate` — schema changes only via Flyway.

## Package layout

Base package: `org.tw.token_billing`

Suggested layers (greenfield — no code yet):

```
org.tw.token_billing
  controller/     REST endpoints
  service/        billing logic
  repository/     Spring Data JPA
  domain/         entities (optional) or map from JPA entities
  dto/            request/response records
  exception/      domain exceptions + @RestControllerAdvice handler
```

Keep new code under `src/main/java/org/tw/token_billing/`. Tests mirror under `src/test/java/`.

## SPDD workflow

Use `/spdd-*` commands with rules in `.cursor/rules/spdd/`. Outputs go to `spdd/analysis/`, `spdd/prompt/`, and `scripts/test-api.sh`.

When implementing, align REASONS prompts and code with domain rules in `token-billing-domain.mdc`.

## Scope reminder (from story)

**In:** `POST /api/usage` only.

**Out:** customer CRUD, bill history queries, automated monthly quota reset jobs.
